IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fcr-dates`
IMPORT `fcr-rules`
IMPORT `fcr-seat`

-- Federal Court Rules 2011 (Cth) -- cases for the party's questions (fcr-seat.l4). Every expected value is worked by
-- hand from the deposited text (Compilation No. 11) with the rule, and never copied from the encoding's output. Day
-- counts are worked in the comments. Calendar: 1 November 2026 is a Sunday; 1 December 2026 a Tuesday; 1 January 2027
-- a Friday; 1 January 2026 a Thursday. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the party to a claim`

§§ `r 1.61 -- counting time`

-- The rule's own Example: "within 3 days from Wednesday ... on or before the following Monday". Wed 4 Nov 2026: Thu 5,
-- Fri 6, (Sat 7, Sun 8 not counted), Mon 9.
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period?` (`the day` 4 11 2026) 3 FALSE EQUALS `the day` 9 11 2026
-- 28 days from Tue 1 Dec 2026: 2-23 Dec is 22 days; 24 Dec to 14 Jan not counted; 15-20 Jan is 6 more: Wed 20 Jan 2027.
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period?` (`the day` 1 12 2026) 28 TRUE EQUALS `the day` 20 1 2027
-- 26 days from Mon 2 Nov 2026 ends Sat 28 Nov: a filing moves to Mon 30 Nov (r 1.61(4)); service does not.
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) 26 TRUE EQUALS `the day` 30 11 2026
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) 26 FALSE EQUALS `the day` 28 11 2026
-- The 5-day edge: 5 days from Fri 6 Nov count business days only: 9, 10, 11, 12, 13 -> Fri 13 Nov. Six days count
-- every day: 7 to 12 -> Thu 12 Nov, a day earlier than five (finding 1).
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period?` (`the day` 6 11 2026) 5 FALSE EQUALS `the day` 13 11 2026
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period?` (`the day` 6 11 2026) 6 FALSE EQUALS `the day` 12 11 2026
-- One day from Wed 23 Dec 2026: 24 Dec to 14 Jan not counted -> Fri 15 Jan 2027.
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period?` (`the day` 23 12 2026) 1 FALSE EQUALS `the day` 15 1 2027
-- 15 days from 20 Dec 2026: 21-23 Dec (3), 15-26 Jan (12) -> Tue 26 Jan 2027, Australia Day: a filing moves to 27 Jan.
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period?` (`the day` 20 12 2026) 15 TRUE EQUALS `the day` 27 1 2027
#ASSERT `What is the last day of my period?` (`the day` 20 12 2026) 15 FALSE EQUALS `the day` 26 1 2027

§§ `r 2.25(3) -- the day a document is filed`

#ASSERT `On what day is my document filed?` (`the day` 9 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS `the day` 9 11 2026
#ASSERT `On what day is my document filed?` (`the day` 9 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS `the day` 10 11 2026
-- Saturday: next business day, Monday.
#ASSERT `On what day is my document filed?` (`the day` 7 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS `the day` 9 11 2026
-- Wed 31 Dec 2025 after 4.30 pm: 1 January is a public holiday -> Fri 2 Jan 2026.
#ASSERT `On what day is my document filed?` (`the day` 31 12 2025) FALSE EQUALS `the day` 2 1 2026

§§ `r 10.32 -- the day of service`

-- Posted Mon 2 Nov 2026: business days 3, 4, 5, 6, 9, 10, 11 -> the seventh is Wed 11 Nov.
#ASSERT `On what day am I served?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) `pre-paid post` EQUALS `the day` 11 11 2026
#ASSERT `On what day am I served?` (`the day` 6 11 2026) `electronic communication` EQUALS `the day` 9 11 2026
#ASSERT `On what day am I served?` (`the day` 9 11 2026) fax EQUALS `the day` 10 11 2026
#ASSERT `On what day am I served?` (`the day` 7 11 2026) `personal service` EQUALS `the day` 7 11 2026

§§ `Part 8 -- starting the claim`

#ASSERT `Must I file a genuine steps statement?` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I file a genuine steps statement?` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `What must go with my originating application?` TRUE `no practice note provides for an alternative document` EQUALS `a statement of claim`
#ASSERT `What must go with my originating application?` FALSE `no practice note provides for an alternative document` EQUALS `a statement of claim or an affidavit`
#ASSERT `What must go with my originating application?` TRUE `a practice note requires an alternative accompanying document` EQUALS `the alternative accompanying document`
#ASSERT `What must go with my originating application?` FALSE `a practice note requires an alternative accompanying document` EQUALS `the alternative accompanying document`
#ASSERT `What must go with my originating application?` TRUE `a practice note permits an alternative accompanying document` EQUALS `the alternative accompanying document or a statement of claim`
#ASSERT `What must go with my originating application?` FALSE `a practice note permits an alternative accompanying document` EQUALS `the alternative accompanying document, a statement of claim or an affidavit`
#ASSERT `Must I state my exemplary damages claim?` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I state my exemplary damages claim?` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- r 8.06: first directions hearing Mon 16 Nov 2026, hearing 30 Nov: back from 16 Nov, business days 13, 12, 11, 10, 9 -> Mon 9 Nov.
#ASSERT `By when must I serve my originating application?` (`the day` 16 11 2026) (`the day` 30 11 2026) EQUALS `the day` 9 11 2026
-- The hearing (Fri 20 Nov) earlier than the directions hearing: back from 20 Nov: 19, 18, 17, 16, 13 -> Fri 13 Nov.
#ASSERT `By when must I serve my originating application?` (`the day` 30 11 2026) (`the day` 20 11 2026) EQUALS `the day` 13 11 2026
-- Across the break: back from Wed 20 Jan 2027: 19, 18, 15 (Jan), then 14 Jan to 24 Dec not counted, 23, 22 Dec -> 22 Dec 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I serve my originating application?` (`the day` 20 1 2027) (`the day` 20 1 2027) EQUALS `the day` 22 12 2026

§§ `rr 16.32, 16.33 -- defence and reply`

-- Served Mon 2 Nov 2026 + 28 = Mon 30 Nov.
#ASSERT `By when must the defence be filed?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) EQUALS `the day` 30 11 2026
-- Served Sat 31 Oct + 28 = Sat 28 Nov, not a business day: filing moves to Mon 30 Nov.
#ASSERT `By when must the defence be filed?` (`the day` 31 10 2026) EQUALS `the day` 30 11 2026
#ASSERT `By when must the defence be filed?` (`the day` 1 12 2026) EQUALS `the day` 20 1 2027
-- Defence served Mon 2 Nov + 14 = Mon 16 Nov.
#ASSERT `By when must I file my reply?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) EQUALS `the day` 16 11 2026

§§ `rr 5.22, 5.23 -- default`

-- Order: statement of claim served, defence filed?, day filed, today, order breached, hearing missed, no due diligence.
-- Filed on the last day (30 Nov): not in default.
#ASSERT `Is the respondent in default?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the day` 30 11 2026) (`the day` 5 12 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Filed a day late (1 Dec): it failed to do the act in the time required (fork F7).
#ASSERT `Is the respondent in default?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the day` 1 12 2026) (`the day` 5 12 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not filed; today is the last day: not yet in default. The day after: in default.
#ASSERT `Is the respondent in default?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) (`the day` 30 11 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the respondent in default?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) (`the day` 1 12 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A defence dated after today is not yet filed.
#ASSERT `Is the respondent in default?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the day` 10 12 2026) (`the day` 1 12 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Christmas: served 1 Dec 2026, last day 20 Jan 2027; on 15 Jan 2027 not yet in default.
#ASSERT `Is the respondent in default?` (`the day` 1 12 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) (`the day` 15 1 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the respondent in default?` (`the day` 1 12 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) (`the day` 21 1 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Defence in time, but the other heads of r 5.22.
#ASSERT `Is the respondent in default?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the day` 30 11 2026) (`the day` 5 12 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the respondent in default?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the day` 30 11 2026) (`the day` 5 12 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the respondent in default?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the day` 30 11 2026) (`the day` 5 12 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- r 5.23(2).
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get on default?` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no order on default, because the respondent is not in default`
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get on default?` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `judgment for the debt or liquidated damages, with interest and costs if appropriate`
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get on default?` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `judgment for the debt or liquidated damages, with interest and costs if appropriate`
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get on default?` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `judgment for the relief claimed in my statement of claim to which the Court is satisfied I am entitled, or for damages to be assessed`
#ASSERT `What judgment can I get on default?` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `judgment for damages to be assessed, or any other order`

-- The duty itself: the defence filed on day 28 of 28 is in time; on day 29 it is not.
#TRACE `r 16.32 -- the respondent must file a defence` 28 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the respondent` DOES `file a defence` AT 28
#ASSERT `r 16.32 -- the defence was filed in time` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 30 11 2026)
#ASSERT (NOT (`r 16.32 -- the defence was filed in time` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 1 12 2026)))

§§ `r 23.21 -- medical examinations`

-- Order: condition in question, party or claimed for, basis.
#ASSERT `Must I attend the medical examination?` TRUE TRUE `an order of the Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I attend the medical examination?` TRUE TRUE `a notice from another party requesting it` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must I attend the medical examination?` TRUE TRUE `neither` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must I attend the medical examination?` FALSE TRUE `an order of the Court` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I bring my own expert to the examination?` TRUE TRUE `a notice from another party requesting it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I bring my own expert to the examination?` TRUE TRUE `an order of the Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I bring my own expert to the examination?` TRUE TRUE `a notice from another party requesting it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I bring my own expert to the examination?` TRUE TRUE `neither` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I bring my own expert to the examination?` TRUE FALSE `a notice from another party requesting it` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must my examination expenses be paid?` TRUE TRUE `a notice from another party requesting it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my examination expenses be paid?` TRUE TRUE `a notice from another party requesting it` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my examination expenses be paid?` TRUE TRUE `an order of the Court` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must my examination expenses be paid?` FALSE TRUE `a notice from another party requesting it` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must I get a copy of the medical report?` TRUE TRUE `a notice from another party requesting it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I get a copy of the medical report?` TRUE TRUE `an order of the Court` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must I get a copy of the medical report?` TRUE FALSE `a notice from another party requesting it` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Part 25 -- offers to settle`

-- Made Mon 2 Nov 2026: 14 days -> Mon 16 Nov is the earliest closing day.
#ASSERT `Is my offer open long enough?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 16 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my offer open long enough?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 15 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Made 20 Dec 2026: 21-23 Dec (3), 15-25 Jan (11) -> Mon 25 Jan 2027.
#ASSERT `Is my offer open long enough?` (`the day` 20 12 2026) (`the day` 25 1 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my offer open long enough?` (`the day` 20 12 2026) (`the day` 24 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Order: made, closing day stated?, closing day, withdrawn, judgment given, day of acceptance.
#ASSERT `Can I still accept the offer?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the day` 16 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the day` 16 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still accept the offer?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the day` 16 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the day` 17 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I still accept the offer?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the day` 1 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still accept the offer?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) FALSE TRUE (`the day` 1 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I still accept the offer?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) TRUE FALSE (`the day` 20 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A stated closing day (10 Nov) shorter than allowed is read up to 16 Nov (fork F11).
#ASSERT `Can I still accept the offer?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the day` 10 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the day` 14 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still accept the offer?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the day` 10 11 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the day` 17 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Before the offer is made there is nothing to accept.
#ASSERT `Can I still accept the offer?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE (`the day` 1 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- r 25.07: made 2 Nov; the 14 days end 16 Nov. Order: made, withdraw day, leave, superseded.
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my offer?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 16 11 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my offer?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 16 11 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my offer?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 5 11 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my offer?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) (`the day` 17 11 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- r 25.04: accepted Mon 2 Nov + 28 = Mon 30 Nov.
#ASSERT `By when must the accepted offer be paid?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `the day` 30 11 2026
#ASSERT `By when must the accepted offer be paid?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the day` 15 12 2026) EQUALS `the day` 15 12 2026
-- Accepted 10 Dec 2026: 11-23 Dec (13), 15-29 Jan (15) -> Fri 29 Jan 2027 (finding 2).
#ASSERT `By when must the accepted offer be paid?` (`the day` 10 12 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `the day` 29 1 2027
-- Accepted Sat 31 Oct + 28 = Sat 28 Nov; payment is not filing, so the day does not move.
#ASSERT `By when must the accepted offer be paid?` (`the day` 31 10 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `the day` 28 11 2026
-- r 25.09. Order: accepted, own time?, own day, paid?, day paid, today, leave.
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my acceptance?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) TRUE (`the day` 30 11 2026) (`the day` 5 12 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my acceptance?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) TRUE (`the day` 1 12 2026) (`the day` 5 12 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my acceptance?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) TRUE (`the day` 1 12 2026) (`the day` 5 12 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my acceptance?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) (`the day` 30 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my acceptance?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) (`the day` 1 12 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my acceptance?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the day` 10 11 2026) FALSE (`the day` 1 1 2026) (`the day` 11 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my acceptance?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) TRUE (`the day` 10 11 2026) TRUE (`the day` 10 11 2026) (`the day` 11 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- r 25.12: made 2 Nov 2026 + 14 = 16 Nov; made 20 Dec 2026 + 14 = 3 Jan 2027 (plain days, fork F13).
#ASSERT `Up to when are my costs covered after accepting?` (`the day` 2 11 2026) EQUALS `the day` 16 11 2026
#ASSERT `Up to when are my costs covered after accepting?` (`the day` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `the day` 3 1 2027
-- r 25.14 cut-off: served Thu 5 Nov -> Fri 6 (1), Mon 9 (2). Served Fri 6 Nov -> Mon 9, Tue 10.
#ASSERT `On what day is the offer costs cut-off?` (`the day` 5 11 2026) EQUALS `the day` 9 11 2026
#ASSERT `On what day is the offer costs cut-off?` (`the day` 6 11 2026) EQUALS `the day` 10 11 2026
-- Served Wed 24 Dec 2025: 25 and 26 Dec public holidays, 27-28 weekend -> Mon 29 (1), Tue 30 (2).
#ASSERT `On what day is the offer costs cut-off?` (`the day` 24 12 2025) EQUALS `the day` 30 12 2025
-- r 25.14 consequences. Order: who made it, accepted, outcome, Court finds unreasonable refusal.
#ASSERT `What costs follow the unaccepted offer?` `the respondent made the offer to me` FALSE `I got judgment less favourable to me than the offer` FALSE EQUALS `I get no costs after the cut-off and must pay the respondent's costs after it on an indemnity basis`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the unaccepted offer?` `the respondent made the offer to me` FALSE `I got judgment as favourable to me as the offer` FALSE EQUALS `rule 25.14 does not apply`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the unaccepted offer?` `the respondent made the offer to me` FALSE `I got judgment more favourable to me than the offer` FALSE EQUALS `rule 25.14 does not apply`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the unaccepted offer?` `the respondent made the offer to me` FALSE `my proceeding was dismissed` TRUE EQUALS `I must pay the respondent's costs, on a party and party basis before the cut-off and an indemnity basis after it`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the unaccepted offer?` `the respondent made the offer to me` FALSE `my proceeding was dismissed` FALSE EQUALS `rule 25.14 does not apply`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the unaccepted offer?` `I made the offer to the respondent` FALSE `I got judgment more favourable to me than the offer` FALSE EQUALS `the respondent must pay my costs, on a party and party basis before the cut-off and an indemnity basis after it`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the unaccepted offer?` `I made the offer to the respondent` FALSE `I got judgment as favourable to me as the offer` FALSE EQUALS `rule 25.14 does not apply`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the unaccepted offer?` `I made the offer to the respondent` FALSE `I got judgment less favourable to me than the offer` FALSE EQUALS `rule 25.14 does not apply`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the unaccepted offer?` `I made the offer to the respondent` FALSE `my proceeding was dismissed` TRUE EQUALS `rule 25.14 does not apply`
#ASSERT `What costs follow the unaccepted offer?` `the respondent made the offer to me` TRUE `I got judgment less favourable to me than the offer` FALSE EQUALS `rule 25.14 does not apply`

