§§ `Part 40 -- costs`

#ASSERT `Who bears the interlocutory costs?` TRUE `the order on the application was in my favour` EQUALS `the Court's costs order governs`
#ASSERT `Who bears the interlocutory costs?` FALSE `the order on the application was in my favour` EQUALS `the costs follow the event: the party the order favours gets them`
#ASSERT `Who bears the interlocutory costs?` FALSE `the order on the application was in the other party's favour` EQUALS `the costs follow the event: the party the order favours gets them`
#ASSERT `Who bears the interlocutory costs?` FALSE `no order was made in favour of any party` EQUALS `they are costs in the cause of whoever succeeds in the proceeding`
-- r 40.08: "less than $100 000". Order: claimed money, awarded, another court more suitable, Admiralty.
#ASSERT `Can my costs be reduced?` TRUE 99999.99 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my costs be reduced?` TRUE 100000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my costs be reduced?` TRUE 100000.01 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my costs be reduced?` FALSE 50000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my costs be reduced?` TRUE 500000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my costs be reduced?` TRUE 50000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I tax my interlocutory costs now?` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I tax my interlocutory costs now?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I tax my interlocutory costs now?` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
